-- title:
--   Transversality of the two branches at a crossing point
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a level-$(N_0,q)$ Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, i.e. the data making the curve `DRLevel.X N₀ q` over `DRLevel.R q` a proper flat integral normal model with the prescribed generic fibre, cusp sections and fibre structure at $q$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\rho_O :$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to O$ a ring homomorphism, and assume the maximal ideal of $O$ is the principal ideal generated by the image of $q$; let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Write $X_O =$ `DRLevel.XO ρO` for the base change of the model along $\rho_O$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product over the geometric fibre of the two component morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O)\,0$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O)\,1$, and let $x_n =$ `𝔛.crossingPt ρO toκ n` be its image in $X_O$ under the first projection followed by the component morphism indexed $0$ followed by the base-change map `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`. Assume the two distinguished points $\xi_\infty =$ `𝔛.ξinf ρO toκ` and $\xi_0 =$ `𝔛.ξzero ρO toκ` of $X_O$ both specialise to $x_n$. For such a specialisation $\xi \rightsquigarrow x$ let `Scheme.branchIdeal` denote the preimage, under the specialisation map $\mathcal O_{X_O,x}\to\mathcal O_{X_O,\xi}$ of stalks, of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X_O,\xi}$. The assertion is that the two branch ideals attached to $\xi_\infty \rightsquigarrow x_n$ and $\xi_0 \rightsquigarrow x_n$ have sum (join of ideals) equal to the whole maximal ideal of the local ring $\mathcal O_{X_O,x_n}$.
--
--   This is the transversality statement at a crossing point of the fibre at $q$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ base changed to $O$: the two branch ideals, cutting out the two components through the crossing, together generate the maximal ideal at that point. It is used in the construction of oriented crossing charts and in the production of a pair of generators of the maximal ideal whose product describes the local equation of the ordinary double point.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel_branchIdeal_xiInf_sup_branchIdeal_xiZero_eq_maximalIdeal.lean

